{"adr":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence","blob_sha256":"47c8903501b5d2fa3c5c72c9c59a5a0eebddae0c8ffa6f4f153f262068b1c16f","body_sha256":"ffea49cb49c014fdadba456a42c77eda38ad5c5ef11af22a599fca427bd42e69","event":"acceptance","obligations":[{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o01","section":"Decision","text":"The stored ADR governance states remain `proposed`, `accepted`, `superseded`, and `rejected`.","text_sha256":"001f7ed52690192b77d47b335e4330ab013d21b545941f42de41184ef734ee5c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o02","section":"Decision","text":"`accepted` is displayed as **Accepted/Planned**: it never implies implementation or verification.","text_sha256":"d610902fd6d5cff09b943043406d1d2b90db998ea93d76ec180c1db0dcd71830"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o03","section":"Decision","text":"Implemented and Verified are derived delivery states, not mutable ADR frontmatter values.","text_sha256":"de7d863ebea816f64cd245d1ca13074476ba5b9ccaaa0d11b15873a0f5e3c105"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o04","section":"Decision","text":"A separate append-only `.codearbiter/decisions/adr-lifecycle.jsonl` is the machine-readable delivery\nledger.","text_sha256":"759cc6fce7eadfbead672933213d2cd616b590254c0c48cc4f0932008aa6e77e"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o05","section":"Decision","text":"Future acceptance appends exactly one immutable acceptance binding for the ADR's canonical\nfull filename stem.","text_sha256":"45c3c7775b4159397b427ae7e332fbd1f309d98a5a22c44f6ebd7a6e4a7aa197"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o06","section":"Decision","text":"That binding records the acceptance commit, the SHA-256 of the exact committed\nGit blob, a separately specified SHA-256 over the immutable decision body, and the digest of a sealed\nauthoritative obligation set.","text_sha256":"46f0d0585671f37c1506509efcda71e744ea4fae40c15bf5886624781c4f5d09"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o07","section":"Decision","text":"A second acceptance binding for the same stem is invalid.","text_sha256":"5f36f155a35f549140829f5d97b66b6c0e703821164ad82cdfaf961d61dae841"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o08","section":"Decision","text":"Each normative obligation has a stable stem-scoped identifier and an exact ADR section/content\nbinding.","text_sha256":"62ff0c9ea9c42e9266c95e9f555db7c92afeff85cfd20fbd62f10c167389038c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o09","section":"Decision","text":"An ADR is Implemented only when every obligation in its sealed set has append-only,\ninput-bound implementation evidence.","text_sha256":"bdd29b07499b0ea78925abccd16aa7bc68babe9ed7dd25ff7f04d6ee1b62824b"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o10","section":"Decision","text":"It is Verified only when every sealed obligation has fresh,\ninput-bound verification evidence produced under an explicit proof contract.","text_sha256":"37e2f1d54e0cd2cab9b5f2fa05f58d2b7ffdc68ef4c30648f1a8804aef9d086e"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o11","section":"Decision","text":"Evidence records bind\nthe source commit, relevant input digests, producer, command or workflow identity, observation time,\nand freshness rule.","text_sha256":"f18a8ac1b5473f4a9baa7ff903ed6d4f77b23b71c6e9bf8220ac154c715937ea"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o12","section":"Decision","text":"Changed inputs invalidate the derived state; they do not rewrite history.","text_sha256":"f15da72d695b8ce858a7e3d79c0c8999fa19c537f533ea28d343ead5e15644ff"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o13","section":"Decision","text":"Public and machine-readable reports expose only obligations that are currently Verified at the input\ndigests being reported.","text_sha256":"4c6e69dd44f9e3cb4d9720e812543a9df8cb4fa930d62d21e865ef0cfd9ae641"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o14","section":"Decision","text":"Unsealed, stale, incomplete, or mismatched obligations fail closed with a\ndiagnostic.","text_sha256":"67235db51f60f946f2f294c6344f1c1da267e4cf7d6cb0bb77d3e228600c3387"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o15","section":"Decision","text":"A repository proof establishes only the narrow repository claim it actually measures; it\ndoes not imply live-host, publication, support, legal, or other external truth without that boundary's\nown approved proof contract.","text_sha256":"f24963b52c4c343b279b06b4dfa803bd81ad65fef66b8a72ba259bdca433b21c"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o16","section":"Decision","text":"Legacy accepted ADRs receive explicit migration `baseline` bindings, never fabricated\nacceptance-time records.","text_sha256":"d92ab8f89a8e7ba7907307e940debc7173793aed00c0f939bab177b9a0595f89"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o17","section":"Decision","text":"Their obligation sets are mapped incrementally and remain unsealed and\nAccepted/Planned until independently reviewed.","text_sha256":"ab10cc734ec0b9fd9bd43dcf067d23ae3b1e4ba1e0d9c00f85cfd9ce659434b5"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o18","section":"Decision","text":"Age, an old pull request, or a matching digest alone\nnever promotes a legacy ADR to Implemented or Verified.","text_sha256":"bb3e961f251a8f72ef5c985335a9e657765a2d080943497c364f4f32bfc50529"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o19","section":"Decision","text":"The canonical ADR identifier remains the full filename stem.","text_sha256":"63914630a3157e123cdbc5beebde43667b1cec00ea5942c7d8d36ed816d29eba"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o20","section":"Decision","text":"Bare-number compatibility remains only\nwhile a number resolves uniquely.","text_sha256":"827fc3460d342bf5ffebe87bbedab937bfc801903d1e491bfa309348af99f64a"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o21","section":"Decision","text":"The two historical `0014` files retain their distinct full-stem\nidentities; neither is renamed or deleted and ambiguous bare-number resolution is never restored.","text_sha256":"b671e2886fc2fd51f3364b6ffad1e90836d9a8e83c6ceeda081b1fa1690bf7ef"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o22","section":"Decision","text":"ADR-0026's already-approved implementation uses ADR-0030's current four-item destructive set:\nlogged bypass (`/override`), merge to the default branch, branch or worktree deletion, and release and\ntag publication.","text_sha256":"e55f9c7d05f712b469749e3b3bd97a89d7ace65ec4718eaa17bb1cbc84be3d1a"},{"id":"0033-bind-accepted-adrs-to-obligation-evidence.o23","section":"Decision","text":"The routing-table registry is authoritative, the arbiter keeps the required resident\nprojection, and CI proves item-for-item parity with a seeded mismatch.","text_sha256":"11c5b925f77cd00d3c8f14f3d8303dc653aabb771f6e73fae6813182eeba155e"}],"obligations_sealed":true,"obligations_sha256":"8a7eb7ec3f9e5cf9c146f89087d62e766e283eac33ad8d642f223089b072a17c","recorded_at":"2026-09-02T11:30:00Z","schema":"adr-lifecycle/v1","source_commit":"455543a6574f4859587641083f05c3c35e64bc82"}
{"schema":"adr-lifecycle/v1","event":"acceptance","adr":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch","recorded_at":"2026-09-05T15:45:55.601Z","source_commit":"e6b9d663888c83ff034a6871a7aa211b41d3d9dd","blob_sha256":"caec3ca7d29942c143661cab268b49cb57bb1c403c55d1ac476ca02a7059e224","body_sha256":"0102347304d5517c66a227fca8118cbdb3f9e465f57c6d72799056c244f97dc0","obligations":[{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.original-publication-ledger","section":"Decision","text":"`.github/published-tags.json` remains exclusively the original-publication receipt ledger. Its\nentries continue to mean that the recorded object identity was captured by the trusted publication\npath; no legacy observation enters that file.","text_sha256":"20b9c2f2a889c12eef400ed3f9e17270f1c036dc2c9e699ad2ba0cc97bbc0bc3"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.closed-legacy-epoch","section":"Decision","text":"A separate, closed `.github/legacy-published-tags.json` records exactly the 44 approved historical\nbaselines observed at 2026-09-04T20:45:43Z.","text_sha256":"89ee1aaa46d38f3b7405550fe7ddf1dd32cefd477586a52ee0b08ab84ed2b641"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.legacy-record-fields","section":"Decision","text":"Each entry records tag name, object SHA, object type,\npeeled commit, observation time, evidence source, and one evidence grade preserving the recovered\ndistinction: 15 `publisher-log-corroborated`, 28 `associated-run-metadata-only`, and one\n`current-release-metadata-only`.","text_sha256":"9f76473a884cefca2a20f4b9577a1065e10b8875a4a2fae15a22d04b5b08a082"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.evidence-grade-preservation","section":"Decision","text":"Each entry records tag name, object SHA, object type,\npeeled commit, observation time, evidence source, and one evidence grade preserving the recovered\ndistinction: 15 `publisher-log-corroborated`, 28 `associated-run-metadata-only`, and one\n`current-release-metadata-only`.","text_sha256":"9f76473a884cefca2a20f4b9577a1065e10b8875a4a2fae15a22d04b5b08a082"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.canonical-approved-set","section":"Decision","text":"The approved identity-and-grade set is the tag-sorted JSON array of objects containing exactly\n`tag`, `evidence_grade`, `source_id`, `object_sha`, `object_type`, and `commit_sha`, encoded as UTF-8\nwith lexicographically sorted object keys and compact JSON separators. Its SHA-256 is\n`26f2d1b06b494dbcc721367e09af52f32ca1a50a71dddb457557af2a48cd8c48`.","text_sha256":"aac5b838bb50fa599445c3c4b4a08260a77f01d36d2ce55a78a4d2ca076d1f4e"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.ledger-provenance-metadata","section":"Decision","text":"The inspected recovery\nmatrix SHA-256 is `cfb3f66e933edb6b1f075f3e089103115c95837b944d56e2c7338d0d3519e8a6`.\nThe ledger identifies this ADR, the observation time, its closed 44-record set, and both digests.","text_sha256":"e83ca7b9b5e8e08a0d48989c5097b06ddd9a200d024e73cff08862d74112f6ea"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.legacy-change-authority","section":"Decision","text":"Adding or replacing a legacy identity or evidence grade requires a new accepted, user-attributed\nADR; release automation and receipt tooling never append to or rewrite the legacy ledger.","text_sha256":"cee9da2498f8e6ef6b88ce0d72e3614ad84cb4fb4d13c5d8f27fee5b968c2dd3"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.receipt-writer-boundary","section":"Decision","text":"Adding or replacing a legacy identity or evidence grade requires a new accepted, user-attributed\nADR; release automation and receipt tooling never append to or rewrite the legacy ledger.","text_sha256":"cee9da2498f8e6ef6b88ce0d72e3614ad84cb4fb4d13c5d8f27fee5b968c2dd3"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.strict-dual-schema-validation","section":"Decision","text":"The immutability guard validates both ledgers strictly, rejects overlap, malformed evidence classes,\nan altered closed-set identity, or an incomplete live inventory, and compares every recorded object\nSHA with the live ref.","text_sha256":"dbc57057a48c1bedf90eacc7f3880f2104de8112c35b116e0a46b90645abb7b6"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.ledger-disjointness","section":"Decision","text":"The immutability guard validates both ledgers strictly, rejects overlap, malformed evidence classes,\nan altered closed-set identity, or an incomplete live inventory, and compares every recorded object\nSHA with the live ref.","text_sha256":"dbc57057a48c1bedf90eacc7f3880f2104de8112c35b116e0a46b90645abb7b6"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.closed-set-integrity","section":"Decision","text":"The immutability guard validates both ledgers strictly, rejects overlap, malformed evidence classes,\nan altered closed-set identity, or an incomplete live inventory, and compares every recorded object\nSHA with the live ref.","text_sha256":"dbc57057a48c1bedf90eacc7f3880f2104de8112c35b116e0a46b90645abb7b6"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.live-inventory-completeness","section":"Decision","text":"The immutability guard validates both ledgers strictly, rejects overlap, malformed evidence classes,\nan altered closed-set identity, or an incomplete live inventory, and compares every recorded object\nSHA with the live ref.","text_sha256":"dbc57057a48c1bedf90eacc7f3880f2104de8112c35b116e0a46b90645abb7b6"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.recorded-object-drift-detection","section":"Risks","text":"This decision is proven wrong if a legacy record is presented as original-publication evidence, a\npost-epoch tag passes strict preflight without a publication receipt, the closed 44-tag set changes\nwithout a new accepted ADR, or a recorded object can move without the guard failing.","text_sha256":"5a7de9fee465387f5b0ece2b36c11c930ff70d18165f0b7ff5cc59aae3d529fa"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.evidence-aware-diagnostics","section":"Decision","text":"Diagnostics and summaries distinguish original-publication receipts from\nlegacy baselines.","text_sha256":"6ee234af98afdb0822508610b51f6dfdf649f3175e8f97a4df0f0893543e9839"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.legacy-mismatch-claim-boundary","section":"Decision","text":"A legacy mismatch states only that the tag moved after its recorded observation;\nit never claims where the tag was originally published.","text_sha256":"6f5d07af7f10b3c146f41301834ba73793cffc74259e82813f63a545a2507f62"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.strict-preflight-union-coverage","section":"Decision","text":"Strict release preflight accepts complete coverage across the disjoint union of the two ledgers only\nwhen every recorded ref matches live state.","text_sha256":"dae89c0998fc1bf5f429bda43787d4c9154b00a9dc09e4a06a2df42d417b5fc7"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.nonlegacy-receipt-gate","section":"Decision","text":"Every tag outside the closed legacy set must have an\noriginal-publication receipt before a later release proceeds.","text_sha256":"0d89d16c09904178d49958a9968b6a67fb555d5f47756c4d7360ef00b89538c0"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.absolute-published-tag-immutability","section":"Decision","text":"The existing prohibition on moving,\nretargeting, or deleting published tags remains absolute, with no break-glass path.","text_sha256":"5aa9ea664cb988e33abd0e0207767e3e1463a6a3dc0984f624558ed7eac4ed41"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.forward-only-provenance-claims","section":"Decision","text":"The accepted residual risk is explicit: a historical tag moved before 2026-09-04T20:45:43Z could be\nfrozen at its later identity. Available evidence neither proves nor disproves such drift. The legacy\nledger establishes a forward immutability guarantee from the recorded observation; it does not\nretroactively prove original publication identity.","text_sha256":"89426467359944604cf719bc48e833ae33bb7b24dd099362da919b13c917d46f"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.corrections-use-new-version","section":"Alternatives considered","text":"- **Reissue or retarget historical tags** \u2014 prohibited because published tags are immutable and a\n  correction must use a new version.","text_sha256":"22e8829ec244876dd2b3effc1c79e9296ca4a57e5023908ee963ef8b0196c8a7"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.release-resumption-gate","section":"Consequences","text":"The release lane can resume after the ADR, separate ledger, guard, documentation, and tests pass the\ngoverned PR and exact-head CI path. Original-publication claims remain uncontaminated. All 44 legacy\nrefs gain durable forward drift detection, and future tags remain receipt-gated.","text_sha256":"eada91e401d12e074699b90426851d7eee0437a336c02d0b525f7c5006149d9c"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.architectural-review-of-closed-set-changes","section":"Consequences","text":"Reviewers must treat changes to the closed legacy set as an architectural change, not a\nroutine receipt reconciliation.","text_sha256":"b6680cade75be89975829a62bf471f16c0e17a8eae2a97e9291dad39eb6ac3d4"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.public-epoch-risk-documentation","section":"Consequences","text":"Public documentation must state the epoch and residual risk without\nimplying historical proof.","text_sha256":"7965c2c35e6a3c55b8293b112d442335ce06cb82b662676e1ffedbc9b8ea5f76"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.prevent-legacy-admission-bypass","section":"Risks","text":"A future change\ncould try to admit a new tag into the closed legacy set to avoid receipt requirements; schema checks,\ntests, governed-path notices, and review must reject that drift.","text_sha256":"631fef92afd75aaea5ded7d2c1576c7ff6748c38047dbabd347166271877e6d7"},{"id":"0034-establish-closed-legacy-published-tag-provenance-epoch.manifest-tooling-schemas-and-diagnostics","section":"Consequences","text":"The guard and manifest tooling must now validate two schemas and render evidence-class-aware\ndiagnostics.","text_sha256":"ddac1bae8ed7907508b97b03eb4352d2d253161b0bc6692f9aff03bb5fc5d1e7"}],"obligations_sha256":"ae0933c619ce0d86f7b405ea35da7763314a966e050e72ae7b84c96df7d1fd18","obligations_sealed":true}
